    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d431">

                <pb facs="0423" n="307" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg307"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.304M28/62.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Bixby, Chief of Engineers, will be officially appointed by the War
                    Department to receive the remains of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>. His
                    place will be taken by the senior officer of the board that has had charge in
                    the raising of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, in case General Bixby can
                    not arrive at Habana in time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
